  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive). Pattern: X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{寄越|よこ}す.\n\nUSAGE:\nThis verb describes things or people being sent toward the speaker. The imperative form {寄越|よこ}せ is commonly used as a blunt demand. The verb always implies movement toward the speaker's location or benefit.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{手紙|てがみ}→手紙：00675_tegami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{寄越|よこ}す (to send a letter)\n- ⟦{返事|へんじ}→返事：00844_henji⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{寄越|よこ}す (to send a reply)\n- ⟦{人|ひと}→人：00476_hito⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{寄越|よこ}す (to send someone over)\n- {寄越|よこ}せ (hand it over — imperative)",
